 **Decision:** `GET /api/status` returns `{ checkedAt, database, redis, workers, queues }` and always 200; each check has a 5 s timeout and a down database or Redis is reported as `"unavailable"` (Redis down → no worker or queue status). Redis is opened fail-fast like the enqueue helpers, with `lazyConnect` and an explicit `connect()` first — with the offline queue disabled a `ping` sent before the socket is ready is rejected, which made a healthy Redis read as unavailable. Queue status is BullMQ's waiting/active/delayed/failed counts plus the newest failed job's time; its `failedReason` (BullMQ stores the raw `error.message`) is shown only when code-shaped (`^[a-z_]+(:[a-z0-9_]+)?$`), else "see the worker log". `/status` renders both tables, refreshes every 30 s and on "Refresh" with the newest response winning, notes that failed counts cover retained jobs only, and is linked from the home page as "9. System status — workers and queues" with no badge (a stopped optional worker is normal).
 **What it affects:** `apps/web/src/lib/status/{loadStatus,format}.ts`, `apps/web/src/app/api/status/route.ts`, `apps/web/src/app/status/`, `apps/web/src/app/page.tsx`.
 
+### D172. Phase 11b verification: a patch replay from main and a real-browser E2E
+**Decision:** The plan's code was written and verified in a draft worktree, then replayed from `main` task by task as test/implementation patches: every task's tests failed before its implementation and passed after it, and the web build (no Edge warnings), `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` (0 warnings), the forced full suite and `git diff --check` passed at every task's state (1979 tests across 17 packages after Task 1; 2107 across 19 after Task 10). The real-browser E2E (headless system Chrome via playwright-core) ran against the built app on `career_intel_test` with `STATUS_STALE_AFTER_MS=5000`, starting the matching worker itself as one `node --import tsx` process — 12 checks passed: Running; all four queues listed; still Running right after a SIGKILL, Stale once 5 s passed; Running after a restart; SIGTERM exits 0 and shows Stopped; and, on a second instance whose database is a closed port, `GET /api/insights` answered 500 with the request-id body and `x-request-id`, its log held exactly one `request_failed` line for that id naming the route, method, path, `AggregateError` and code `ECONNREFUSED`, with no message text, and no raw Next.js error print.
+**Found while building, not by the original tests:** the double-signal shutdown crash (D170), the Edge-runtime instrumentation warning (D169), the offline-queue `ping` that made a healthy Redis read as unavailable (D171), and the `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` lint error on the status page's polling (fixed with the codebase's promise-chain pattern).
+**What it affects:** the E2E script in `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-07-phase-11b-logging-monitoring/e2e/`.
+
 *Entries are appended chronologically. Do not edit or delete past entries when a decision is later reversed — add a new entry that supersedes it and cross-reference the original.*
